            A navbar uses only a few tags: <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> wraps it,
            <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> hold the list,
            <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> is a link that goes somewhere, and
            <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> does something. The trap is
            <b>link vs. button</b>: use <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> to navigate,
            <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> to trigger an action. Test yourself.
