          <p>
            This is the single most important thing the brief skips. A navbar is
            a row, and that row is built with <b>flexbox</b>. Set
            <code>display:flex</code> on the container and its children sit in a
            line. Then <code>justify-content</code> decides how they spread
            along the row, and <code>gap</code> sets the space between them.
            Change them and watch.
