          <h3>How <code>:hover</code> and transitions work</h3>
          <p>
            The bonus asks for a hover effect but never explains the mechanism.
            <code>:hover</code> is a <b>pseudo-class</b> — a second set of
            styles the browser applies only while the pointer is over the
            element. Add <code>transition</code> and the change eases in instead
            of snapping. Pick an effect, set the speed, and hover the link.
          </p>

