        <!-- ===================== s08 READING AI CODE ===================== -->
        <section class="section" id="s08" data-nav="Reading AI code">
          <span class="part-badge">Part 08</span>
          <h3>Reading code you didn't write</h3>
          <p>
            The brief tells you to accept, reject, or simplify the AI's answer —
            but not how to judge it. You cannot accept or reject code you cannot
            read. Run every AI snippet through four questions:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <b>Does it nest correctly?</b> Every opening tag has a matching
              close, indented sensibly.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Is anything unused?</b> Wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>s,
              classes, or features you never asked for.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Do the selectors hit real elements?</b> A CSS rule for
              <code>.navbar__cta</code> is dead if no element has that class.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Is it the right element?</b> A link (<code>&lt;a&gt;</code>)
              for navigation, a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> for an action.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <pre class="code"><span class="c">// the same navbar, annotated</span>
<span class="keep">&lt;nav class="navbar"&gt;</span>            <span class="keep">// keep — semantic, one clear wrapper</span>
  <span class="cut">&lt;div class="inner-wrap"&gt;</span>      <span class="cut">// cut  — an extra box doing nothing</span>
    <span class="keep">&lt;a class="brand"&gt;ZS One&lt;/a&gt;</span>   <span class="keep">// keep</span>
    <span class="cut">&lt;input placeholder="Search"&gt;</span> <span class="cut">// cut  — never in the plan</span>
    <span class="keep">&lt;a class="cta"&gt;Play Now&lt;/a&gt;</span>    <span class="keep">// keep — the one action</span>
  <span class="cut">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
<span class="keep">&lt;/nav&gt;</span></pre>

          <div class="callout">
            <b>Simplify by default.</b> If you cannot explain what a line does,
            do not keep it. Fewer lines you understand beat more lines you
            don't.
          </div>
        </section>

